# Windows environment template (no secrets)

Copy to `C:\Zedral\config\backend.env` on the server and fill secrets via DPAPI / Credential Manager.
The WinSW service loads this file (or equivalent env vars set on the service).

```
NODE_ENV=production
DEPLOY_TARGET=windows
HOST=127.0.0.1
PORT=3001
LOG_DIR=C:\Zedral\logs
LOG_LEVEL=info

# Loopback PostgreSQL — use m1_app with a vaulted password (never tubemill:tubemill)
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://m1_app:CHANGE_ME@127.0.0.1:5432/zedral_prod

TENANT_ID=00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001
COLLECTOR_MODE=sim
BC_ADAPTER=file

SUPERTOKENS_CONNECTION_URI=http://127.0.0.1:3567
SUPERTOKENS_API_KEY=CHANGE_ME

SERVICE_TOKEN=CHANGE_ME_LONG_RANDOM
AUTH_STRICT=true
# Plant host + Capacitor WebView origins (operator APK). Do not use same-origin when APK is deployed.
CORS_ORIGIN=https://YOUR_PLANT_HOST,https://localhost,capacitor://localhost

API_DOMAIN=https://YOUR_PLANT_HOST
WEBSITE_DOMAIN=https://YOUR_PLANT_HOST
API_BASE_PATH=/api/auth
WEBSITE_BASE_PATH=/auth
```
